irculation (the network simplex): a source feeds each left vertex up to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"capacity, each edge of positive weight carries one unit at the cost of minus its weight,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each right vertex drains into a sink up to its capacity, and the sink returns to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"source. Edges of weight zero or less are never taken. Parallel edges are distinct and may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both be taken. Which optimum is returned when several exist is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order and ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per edge in position order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That of the network simplex on n + 2 vertices and n + m + 1 arcs; polynomial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in practice, O(n² m) in the worst case of its pivots."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition"},{"text":" is this graph’s; every capacity is at least zero and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"capacities fit in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":"; |weight| fits the network simplex’s cost bound (4(n + 3)(the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"greatest weight + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"d